"help.start.title" = "Getting started";
"help.start.body" = "In macOS System Settings → Appearance, select Light or Dark to turn off the system’s automatic appearance schedule. Choose a city and offsets, then enable automatic switching. On first use, allow Dusk Shift to control System Events.";
"help.offset.title" = "Sunrise and sunset offsets";
"help.offset.body" = "Adjust sunrise and sunset independently by up to 120 minutes in either direction, in 1-minute steps. The slider center means on time. At sunrise, left delays light mode and right brings it forward. At sunset, left delays dark mode and right brings it forward. Negative input means earlier; positive means later. Valid input previews immediately and applies when you release the slider, press Return, or leave the field. Reset restores a zero offset.";
"help.city.title" = "Cities, time zones, and offline use";
"help.city.body" = "Times use the selected city’s time zone and local date, including daylight saving changes. Sunrise and sunset are calculated on this Mac, with no network or location permission needed. Change the city manually when traveling. This version supports the built-in city list.";
"help.sleep.title" = "Switching and wake recovery";
"help.sleep.body" = "Sunrise switches to Light and sunset switches to Dark. On launch and wake, Dusk Shift checks and restores the scheduled appearance. Pausing or quitting keeps the last appearance. Keep the app running for scheduled switches; this version does not yet support launch at login.";
"help.polar.title" = "Special dates and accuracy";
"help.polar.body" = "Polar day defaults to Light and polar night to Dark. Offsets that cross adjacent switch boundaries are limited or skipped, with a notice in settings. Calculations use standard astronomical conditions; terrain, elevation, and weather can affect what you observe.";
"help.privacy.title" = "Permissions and privacy";
"help.privacy.body" = "If switching fails, allow Dusk Shift to control System Events in System Settings → Privacy & Security → Automation, then retry on the Automatic switching tab. Your city, offsets, language, and enabled state are stored locally and are not uploaded.";
